h-ai-denton-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI", "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI - Denton, Texas, United States Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI - Denton, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI 515177 Denton, Texas, United States Faculty Closing on: Jun 1 2027 Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health \u2013 Biostatistics/Health AI Employee Classification: Assistant/Associate Professor Campus: University of North Texas Division: UNT-Provost SubDivision-Department: UNT-Col of Publ Affairs & Hlth Sci Department: UNT-Rehabilitation and Health Serv-135350 Job Location: Denton Salary: Compensation is competitive and commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and discipline, in accordance with university guidelines and available funding. FTE: 1.00 Retirement Eligibility: ORP Eligible About Us - Values Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The Department of Rehabilitation & Health Services (RHS) is a community-engaged academic unit providing research and education that reaches beyond the classroom. Faculty with expertise in public health, applied gerontology, health services, rehabilitation counseling, substance use, and behavioral health conduct innovative research that impacts our community and prepares students for a career making a positive change in the lives of others. Our graduates pursue careers as researchers, health professionals, educators, administrators, and clinicians committed to improving the lives of those they serve. The department is part of the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences (PAHS) that prepares graduates to address diverse and complex social issues such as aging, disability, disaster management and recovery, criminal justice, health disparities and public safety, and find solutions to challenges in public administration, public and mental health, exercise physiology, and urban design. We have nine academic departments with undergraduate and graduate programs, the Kristin Farmer Autism Center, the Center for Public Management, the UNT Speech and Hearing Center, the UNT Work Inclusion and Supported Employment (UNTWISE) program, UNT ELEVAR, and several professional development and clinical training programs to facilitate careers to address a global society. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The Department of Rehabilitation & Health Services (RHS) in the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences at the University of North Texas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Public Health with expertise in biostatistics and/or health artificial intelligence (AI). All areas of biostatistics will be considered. We seek an accomplished scholar whose research leverages advanced statistical methods, artificial intelligence, machine learning, or computational analytics to address complex public health challenges. The successful candidate will bring a vision for advancing data-driven discovery while mentoring the next generation of public health scientists and for the rank of Associate Professor will bring an established, externally funded research program. This is an exceptional opportunity to join a collaborative, interdisciplinary research environment at one of the nation's leading public research universities, where innovation, partnership, student success, and translational impact are central to our mission. The successful candidate will: \u2022Lead and expand a nationally recognized, externally funded research program in biostatistics, health AI, or related areas. \u2022Teach graduate and undergraduate courses in biostatistics, epidemiology, health data science, artificial intelligence, and related disciplines. \u2022Mentor master's and doctoral students while fostering a collaborative and innovative research environment. \u2022Develop interdisciplinary collaborations that advance the application of statistics, AI and/or advanced analytics to public health research and practice. \u2022Publish impactful research in leading peer-reviewed journals and present findings at national and international conferences. \u2022At the Rank of Associate Professor, provide leadership in curriculum development, faculty mentoring, and strategic initiatives. \u2022Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service. Preferred Areas of Research All areas of biostatistics will be considered, but we welcome applicants whose research aligns with biostatistics and health AI, including but not limited to: \u2022 Artificial intelligence and machine learning for public health \u2022 Biostatistical methods development \u2022 Bayesian statistics \u2022 Predictive modeling and risk prediction \u2022 Precision public health \u2022 Population health analytics \u2022 Causal inference and advanced epidemiologic methods \u2022 Clinical and public health informatics \u2022 Big data analytics \u2022 Electronic health record (EHR) research \u2022 Natural language processing in healthcare \u2022 Geospatial and spatial statistics \u2022 Design and analysis of cohort studies, case-control studies, randomized clinical trials and/or intervention studies \u2022 Sample size and power analysis \u2022 Analytic strategies for high dimensional -omics studies \u2022 Health equity through data science \u2022 Explainable and trustworthy AI for healthcare \u2022 Data visualization and decision support systems Applicants utilizing innovative computational approaches, high-performance computing, federated learning, or multidisciplinary research methods are especially encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Public Health, Biostatistics, Statistics, Data Science, Epidemiology, Computer Science, Health Informatics, or a closely related discipline. For the rank of Assistant Professor ABD will be considered but candidates must hold degree at the time of appointment. For the rank of Associate Professor, qualifications for appointment with tenure. An established record of peer-reviewed publications demonstrating scholarly excellence. Evidence of a sustained (Associate Professor), or potential for (Assistant Professor), externally funded research program. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Experience mentoring graduate students and early-career researchers (for consideration at the Rank of Associate Professor). Preferred Qualifications National or international recognition in biostatistics, health AI, or population health analytics. Ongoing and transferable externally funded research grants Experience leading interdisciplinary research teams. Demonstrated success in developing collaborations with healthcare systems, government agencies, or industry partners. Experience integrating AI and advanced analytics into public health education. Demonstrated leadership in academic programs, professional organizations, or large collaborative research initiatives. Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions 1. Cover Letter expressing your interest and qualification for the position. If applying for the rank of Associate Professor emphasis should be placed on your qualifications for the rank. 2. Current Curriculum Vitae 3. A research statement highlighting your past research accomplishments and an outline of your 5-year research plan including on-going or future external funding that would continue/occur at UNT. 4. Statement of Teaching Philosophy 5. References \u2013 List of Names and Contact Information (email and phone) for at least 3 (no more than 6) professional references. References will be contacted only if selected for an on-campus interview. Questions can be directed to search committee chair, Dr. Chisom Iwundu at chisom.iwundu@unt.edu. Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation or proceeding. Apply for This Job First Name (required) eee4ad10 Last Name (required) 00b2c885 Email (required) 244548fa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 2ec29f4c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments UNT-Provost UNT-Provost Locations Denton, Texas, United States Denton, Texas, United States First Name (required) 2152eaf1 Last Name (