ines. Individuals will manage work teams of custodians to achieve cleaning goals, including managing interpersonal conflicts and resolving disputes. Individuals will regularly inspect assigned facilities and equipment to ensure that cleaning standards are maintained and equipment is functioning appropriately. Individuals will assist in the hiring and training of team members. Individuals will participate in activities and functions as directed by the leadership of the department. Non-Student Hourly Research We provide a high-quality education to our diverse student population through excellence and innovation in teaching and research in order to serve the scientific and engineering needs of the state of Texas and the nation. This will be achieved by a balance of formal course work, practical laboratory training, and research projects that encompass both the basic science and the applied aspects of materials science and engineering. Before you leave, please sign up for our talent network! First Name (required) 3b817ace Last Name (required) f1159530 Email (required) aa1077e7 Phone Number (optional) be841c6e 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) \u00c5land Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Cura\u00e7ao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic (+1) Ecuador (+593) Egypt (+20) El Salvador (+503) Equatorial Guinea (+240) Eritrea (+291) Estonia (+372) Eswatini (+268) Ethiopia (+251) Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) (+500) Faroe Islands (+298) Fiji (+679) Finland (+358) France (+33) French Guiana (+594) French Polynesia (+689) Gabon (+241) Gambia (+220) Georgia (+995) Germany (+49) Ghana (+233) Gibraltar (+350) Greece (+30) Greenland (+299) Grenada (+1) Guadeloupe (+590) Guam (+1) Guatemala (+502) Guernsey (+44) Guinea (+224) Guinea-Bissau (+245) Guyana (+592) Haiti (+509) Honduras (+504) Hong Kong (+852) Hungary (+36) Iceland (+354) India (+91) Indonesia (+62) Iran (+98) Iraq (+964) Ireland (+353) Isle of Man (+44) Israel (+972) Italy (+39) Jamaica (+1) Japan (+81) Jersey (+44) Jordan (+962) Kazakhstan (+7) Kenya (+254) Kiribati (+686) Kosovo (+383) Kuwait (+965) Kyrgyzstan (+996) Laos (+856) Latvia (+371) Lebanon (+961) Lesotho (+266) Liberia (+231) Libya (+218) Liechtenstein (+423) Lithuania (+370) Luxembourg (+352) Macao (+853) Madagascar (+261) Malawi (+265) Malaysia (+60) Maldives (+960) Mali (+223) Malta (+356) Marshall Islands (+692) Martinique (+596) Mauritania (+222) Mauritius (+230) Mayotte (+262) Mexico (+52) Micronesia (+691) Moldova (+373) Monaco (+377) Mongolia (+976) Montenegro (+382) Montserrat (+1) Morocco (+212) Mozambique (+258) Myanmar (Burma) (+95) Namibia (+264) Nauru (+674) Nepal (+977) Netherlands (+31) New Caledonia (+687) New Zealand (+64) Nicaragua (+505) Niger (+227) Nigeria (+234) Niue (+683) Norfolk Island (+672) North Korea (+850) North Macedonia (+389) Northern Mariana Islands (+1) Norway (+47) Oman (+968) Pakistan (+92) Palau (+680) Palestine (+970) Panama (+507) Papua New Guinea (+675) Paraguay (+595) Peru (+51) Philippines (+63) Poland (+48) Portugal (+351) Puerto Rico (+1) Qatar (+974) R\u00e9union (+262) Romania (+40) Russia (+7) Rwanda (+250) Samoa (+685) San Marino (+378) S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9 & Pr\u00edncipe (+239) Saudi Arabia (+966) Senegal (+221) Serbia (+381) Seychelles (+248) Sierra Leone "}, "https://careers.untsystem.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-supply-chain-management-denton-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management", "description": "Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management - Denton, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management - Denton, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management 515016 Denton, Texas, United States Faculty Title: Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management Employee Classification: Asst Professor Campus: University of North Texas Division: UNT-Provost SubDivision-Department: UNT-Ryan College of Business Department: UNT-Supply Chain Management-131350 Job Location: Denton Salary: Compensation is competitive and commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and discipline, in accordance with university guidelines and available funding. FTE: 1.00 Retirement Eligibility: ORP Eligible About Us - Values Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The University of North Texas is a Carnegie R1 research university located in Denton, Texas, within the vibrant and rapidly growing Dallas\u2013Fort Worth metropolitan area. The G. Brint Ryan College of Business is accredited by AACSB International and offers undergraduate, master\u2019s, doctoral, and professional programs designed to prepare students for leadership in an increasingly complex global economy. The Department of Supply Chain Management is an academic department within the G. Brint Ryan College of Business at the University of North Texas. The department\u2019s mission is to advance supply chain knowledge and practice through impactful research, innovative education, meaningful industry engagement, and the development of students who are prepared to lead in complex and rapidly changing organizations. The department offers academic programs at the bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral levels. Its undergraduate portfolio includes the Bachelor of Science in Supply Chain Management with concentrations in Logistics, Operations Management, Aviation Logistics, Purchasing, and Supply Chain Analytics. The department also supports the Bachelor of Science in Industrial Distribution. UNT\u2019s supply chain programs are distinguished by innovative curricula, experiential learning, strong employer relationships, and extensive engagement with the Dallas\u2013Fort Worth business community. The undergraduate supply chain program was ranked No. 4 in Gartner\u2019s 2024 Supply Chain University Top 25, reflecting its academic quality, industry relevance, and commitment to preparing students for successful careers. Department faculty conduct basic and applied research across a broad range of supply chain topics, including logistics, sourcing and procurement, operations management, transportation, supply chain analytics, technology, resilience, risk, sustainability, and complex systems. Faculty members publish in leading academic journals, collaborate with industry and government partners, mentor doctoral students, and contribute leadership to major professional and scholarly organizations. The department benefits from its relationship with the Center for Logistics & Supply Chain Management and the Center for Strategic Sourcing. These partnerships support student development, industry engagement, applied research, executive education, scholarships, internships, and collaboration with organizations throughout the Dallas\u2013Fort Worth region and beyond. UNT\u2019s location in one of North America\u2019s most important logistics and distribution hubs provides exceptional opportunities for research, teaching, and industry collaboration. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The Department of Supply Chain Management in the University of North Texas G. Brint Ryan College of Business invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management. The anticipated appointment will begin Fall 2027 and will be based primarily on the UNT Denton campus. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of high-quality research with the potential for publication in leading supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or related business journals. The candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses, contribute to the department\u2019s academic programs, mentor students, and participate in service activities appropriate to rank. The department welcomes candidates whose research and teaching interests fall within supply chain management. Areas of particular interest may include: \u2022 Logistics and transportation \u2022 Sourcing, procurement, and supplier management \u2022 Operations and process management \u2022 Supply chain analytics and artificial intelligence \u2022 Supply chain technology and digital transformation \u2022 Sustainability and circular supply chains \u2022 Aviation logistics \u2022 Humanitarian, healthcare, public-sector, or defense supply chains Candidates with complementary expertise that strengthens or expands the department\u2019s existing capabilities are also encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to: \u2022 Develop and sustain a productive, high-quality research program with the potential for publication in leading peer-reviewed journals. \u2022 Teach supply chain management and related courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. \u2022 Deliver courses in face-to-face, online, hybrid, or other formats consistent with departmental needs. \u2022 Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of departmental curricula and academic programs. \u2022 Mentor undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. \u2022 Collaborate with faculty members on research, teaching, and program initiatives. \u2022 Pursue external research funding or industry-supported research when appropriate. \u2022 Engage constructively with the department\u2019s industry partners, centers, alumni, and professional communities. \u2022 Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service. \u2022 Support the university\u2019s commitment to student success and an inclusive learning and working environment. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 A doctoral degree in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, purchasing, transportation, industrial engineering, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited institution by the time of appointment, or have equivalent applied experience in accordance with faculty credentialing guidelines \u2022 Evidence of the ability or potential to conduct high-quality scholarly research. \u2022 Evidence of the ability or potential to publish in respected peer-reviewed journals. \u2022 Evidence of the ability or potential to provide effective university-level instruction. \u2022 Strong communication skills. \u2022 Candidates who are ABD will be considered, provided that all doctoral degree requirements are completed before the appointment begins. Employees in this job may be responsible for conducting research on, working on, or having the ability to access critical organizational infrastructure and they must be able to maintain the security and integrity of the infrastructure related to this role. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates who demonstrate: \u2022 A clearly defined research agenda with strong potential for publication in leading journals. \u2022 Publications or manuscripts under advanced review in recognized supply chain management, logistics, operations, or related journals. \u2022 Expertise that complements the department\u2019s existing research and teaching strengths. \u2022 Experience teaching supply chain management or related courses. \u2022 The ability to teach across multiple levels and instructional formats. \u2022 Experience working with doctoral students or participating in doctoral education. \u2022 Potential to secure external research support. \u2022 Interest in interdisciplinary, industry-engaged, or applied research. \u2022 Experience developing relationships with companies, government agencies, professional associations, or other external organizations. \u2022 A record of collegiality and the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions Applicants must submit a minimum of two professional references as part of their application. If needed, additional references can be added after the application has been submitted. Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation 