ion: Senior Lecturer Campus: University of North Texas Division: UNT-Provost SubDivision-Department: UNT-Col of Merch, Hosp & Tour Department: UNT-Hospitality & Tourism-137310 Job Location: Denton Salary: Compensation is competitive and commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and discipline, in accordance with university guidelines and available funding. FTE: 1.00 Retirement Eligibility: ORP Eligible About Us - Values Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The mission of the Department of Hospitality and Tourism Management is to educate the next generation of hospitality and tourism leaders who strive for excellence and embrace innovation within a caring and empowering community. The program offers a Bachelor of Science in Hospitality Management in Denton and Frisco, a Bachelor of Science in Event Design and Experience Management in Denton and Frisco, a Master of Science in Hospitality Management, a Master of Science in Hospitality & Tourism Data Analytics. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The Department of Hospitality, Event and Tourism Management in the G. Brint Ryan College of Business at the University of North Texas (UNT) invites applications for a faculty member at the rank of Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (non-tenure track) in Event Design and Experience Management or closely aligned fields. The successful candidate will work closely with the Department of Hospitality, Event and Tourism Management (HETM) Chair and faculty members to offer an innovative curriculum utilizing the latest technology and best practices for onsite and virtual events, enhance the undergraduate experience, grow program enrollments, grow industry connections, and lead and execute signature student led events which showcase and represent the Department in an exceptional manner and also prepare students for careers in the event management industry with a proposed start date of January 16, 2027. The faculty member will develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses (if possessing a terminal degree), primarily in the Event Design and Experience Management curriculum, as well as courses in Hospitality Management, on the main UNT Denton campus and may also teach on the Frisco campus as needed; build partnerships with the hospitality industry to enhance class events, projects, jobs, and internship opportunities for students; mentor student groups and organizations, as appropriate; participate in university, department, and school committees and other service. The successful candidate will be involved in internal and external collaborations and will lead student study tours. Minimum Qualifications Earned masters degree in Event Management/Hospitality Management/Hospitality Administration/; OR consideration will be given to a closely aligned masters degree with evidence of graduate coursework in the event management/hospitality field. At least three years of professional event management industry experience. Excellent teaching skills; excellent communication skills; clear devotion to students and the missions of higher education. Ability to connect with industry partners particularly in events related entities and develop those relationships for the benefit of the college and students. Evidence of three or more years in industry experience and connections including a record of working in the event, hospitality, club, resort, tourism, attraction, or related industries. A team player who demonstrates leadership, integrity, and collegiality. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated excellence in teaching. Knowledge of and connections to event related industry organizations like PCMA, MPI, IAEE, etc. Possess current event related industry certification such as Certified Meeting Planner, Certified in Exhibition Management, etc. Previous experience executing events particularly corporate and fundraising events. Experience/coursework in distributed learning/web based course development and delivery. Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions Applicants must submit a minimum of two professional references as part of their application. If needed, additional references can be added after the application has been submitted. Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation or proceeding. Apply for This Job First Name (required) 6af81e34 Last Name (required) 7a807dd7 Email (required) 705f5ee3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 4bebfe59 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments UNT-Provost UNT-Provost Locations Denton, Texas, United States Denton, Texas, United States First Name (required) 843f877f Last Name (required) eef98b41 Email (required) b13e3cea Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) f67f88da Last Name (required) c2bc09f1 Email (required) 97a6aa46 Share to: d6edca4e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Recommended Jobs CAAAM Lab Assistant The CAAAM Lab Assistant role assists with experiments using techniques such as optical microscopy, profilometry, hardness testing, and density measurements, and helps translate experimental results into graphs and schematics. Additional responsibilities include maintaining laboratory inventory, coordinating incoming and outgoing packages, and following established laboratory safety practices. The ideal candidate will work effectively in a collaborative team environment, adapt to changing priorities, and demonstrate the ability to quickly learn new techniques and research solutions using relevant scientific literature. Completion of required UNT Lab Safety training is expected prior to beginning laboratory work. This is a temporary position with a start date of January 4, 2027 and ends on May 28, 2027 Office Support Assistant (Night Desk Clerk) The Office Support Assistant serves the full time staff member at the front desk overnight, providing a welcoming, safe, and secure environment for residents of the community. This position reports crisis and maintenance issues to on-call staff while providing customer support and other administrative follow-up. Custodian This position\u2019s purpose is to serve as a custodian for the Department of Housing and Residence Life. This is an essential position, maintaining essential operations during emergencies and university closures. The custodian will maintain a standard of cleanliness, sanitation, safety and standard of excellence in all assigned buildings (Residence Halls, Dining Areas, and Other Buildings). Associate Registrar This position is responsible for strategic oversight of Certifications and Degree Conferral, including planning, organizing, and ensuring continuity and continuous improvement of processes, systems, and student services including the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Involved in new initiatives with colleagues across campus related to enrollment and retention to ensure successful implementation. Oversees operations of multiple functional areas and works directly with staff for ongoing professional development and the implementation of new initiatives, and/or updated systems, policies, and processes. Advises students, parents, faculty and staff about departmental and university regulations. Requires discernment to resolve complex escalations and implement proactive solutions. This position manages teams within the Office of the Registrar, collaborates across the division, and with faculty and staff throughout the University. Works to ensure the accuracy and integrity of academic and student data, and compliance with a range of institutional, state, and federal regulations. Responsible for collaboration across teams to achieve a collective outcome that optimizes results and impact that directly affects enrollment and retention. Custodial Services Supervisor This is an essential position, who's primary purpose is to provide direct supervision of the day-to-day operations of custodial staff within the residence halls, residential dining areas, and assigned auxiliary buildings. Supervisory responsibilities include: approving leave, managing time and attendance. Additionally, individuals will provide training, instruction, and coaching. Individuals will apply progressive discipline to subordinate staff as needed, in accordance with university, system, state and federal guidelines. Individuals will manage work teams of custodians to achieve cleaning goals, including managing interpersonal conflicts and resolving disputes. Individuals will regularly inspect assigned facilities and equipment to ensure that cleaning standards are maintained and equipment is functioning appropriately. Individuals will assist in the hiring and training of team members. Individuals will participate in activities and functions as directed by the leadership of the department. Non-Student Hourly Research We provide a high-quality education to our diverse student population through excellence and innovation in teaching and research in order to serve the scientific and engineering needs of the state of Texas and the nation. This will be achieved by a balance of formal course work, practical laboratory training, and research projects that encompass both the basic science and the applied aspects of materials science and engineering. Before you leave, please sign up for our talent network! First Name (required) 69ae9488 Last Name (required) a838dadb Email (required) 87353311 Phone Number (optional) 0963b709 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) \u00c5land Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda