lues Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The UNT Department of Psychology is one of the largest and most dynamic psychology programs in the region, home to more than 40 faculty members, 100 graduate students, and over 2,500 undergraduate majors. Our faculty lead innovative research programs spanning clinical science, counseling psychology, cognitive and brain sciences, developmental psychology, health psychology, and social and behavioral health. Through mentorship, hands-on research training, and interdisciplinary collaboration, our students develop the knowledge and experience needed to succeed in academia, healthcare, industry, and public service. The Department of Psychology is housed within the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences (PAHS). PAHS prepares graduates to address diverse and complex social issues such as aging, disability, disaster management and recovery, criminal justice, health disparities, behavioral health, and public safety, and find solutions to challenges in public administration, public and mental health, exercise physiology, and urban design. PAHS has nine academic departments with undergraduate and graduate programs, and is also the home for several centers such as the UNT Center for Sport Psychology and Athlete Mental Health, the UNT Psychology Clinic, the Center for Psychosocial Health Disparities Research, the Kristin Farmer Autism Center, the Center for Public Management, the UNT Speech and Hearing Center, the UNT Work Inclusion and Supported Employment (UNTWISE) program, UNT ELEVAR (Empower, Learn, Excel, enVision, Advance, Rise), and several professional development and clinical training programs to facilitate careers to address a global society. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The Department of Psychology in the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences at the University of North Texas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Counseling Psychology to join our APA-accredited doctoral program. The specific area of research for this faculty position is open, although we are particularly interested in candidates whose work would strengthen the program\u2019s Sport Psychology cluster. Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate a strong research program and a record of applying for or receiving extramural funding. Faculty responsibilities include developing and maintaining an active research program, teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, seeking research grants, advising and mentoring doctoral students, and sharing service duties. Successful applicants are also expected to demonstrate strong interests in mentoring students\u2019 professional development and supervising students\u2019 clinical work since mentoring and supervision are valued components of program faculty. This is an exceptional opportunity to join one of the nation's leading public research universities, where interdisciplinary collaboration, community engagement, and research with real-world impact are central to our mission. The successful candidate will: \u2022 Develop and sustain an externally funded research program in counseling psychology. \u2022 Teach undergraduate and doctoral-level courses in counseling psychology and related areas. \u2022 Mentor doctoral students in research, clinical training, and professional development. \u2022 Supervise doctoral research, including master's theses and doctoral dissertations. \u2022 Contribute to doctoral clinical training through practicum supervision and other training experiences consistent with the faculty member's expertise. \u2022 Publish impactful research in leading peer-reviewed journals and present findings at national and international conferences. \u2022 Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to advance research that promotes psychological health, resilience, and well-being. \u2022 Contribute to curriculum development, APA accreditation activities, departmental governance, and professional service. Applicants employing innovative methodologies \u2014including community-engaged research, longitudinal studies, implementation science, digital mental health technologies, mixed-methods research, advanced quantitative methods, or intervention research\u2014are especially encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research would strengthen the program\u2019s Sport Psychology cluster and whose professional expertise would contribute to the UNT Center for Sport Psychology and Athlete Mental Health. Relevant areas may include sport and performance psychology; athlete mental health, wellness, identity, and help-seeking; and related prevention or intervention work. Strong candidates whose research complements the program\u2019s other elective clusters or existing program strengths will also be considered. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 Ph.D. in Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program or a closely related discipline. \u2022 Eligibility for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Texas. \u2022 Evidence of a strong and growing research agenda with potential for sustained external funding. \u2022 Demonstrated record of scholarly publications. \u2022 Commitment to excellence in teaching, mentoring, and training students. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Record of applying for and/or receiving competitive extramural funding. \u2022 Research program and expertise that complement one or more of the program\u2019s three elective clusters, with particular interest in candidates who would strengthen the Sport Psychology cluster. \u2022 Record of teaching/mentoring undergraduate or graduate students. \u2022 For candidates with Sport Psychology expertise, certification or eligibility for certification as a Certified Mental Performance Consultant (CMPC) through the Association for Applied Sport Psychology (AASP). Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions Applicant Documents \u2022 Cover Letter \u2022 Curriculum Vitae \u2022 Statement of Teaching Philosophy \u2022 Statement of Research Interests, Accomplishments, and Future Plans \u2022 Up to three representative publications \u2022 References \u2013 List of Names and Contact Information for 3 individuals Review of applications will begin on 10/15/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation or proceeding. Apply for This Job First Name (required) b1922692 Last Name (required) f8083b9c Email (required) 5e19b0f1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 9f53e7e3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can sel