, and compliance with a range of institutional, state, and federal regulations. Responsible for collaboration across teams to achieve a collective outcome that optimizes results and impact that directly affects enrollment and retention. Custodial Services Supervisor This is an essential position, who's primary purpose is to provide direct supervision of the day-to-day operations of custodial staff within the residence halls, residential dining areas, and assigned auxiliary buildings. Supervisory responsibilities include: approving leave, managing time and attendance. Additionally, individuals will provide training, instruction, and coaching. Individuals will apply progressive discipline to subordinate staff as needed, in accordance with university, system, state and federal guidelines. Individuals will manage work teams of custodians to achieve cleaning goals, including managing interpersonal conflicts and resolving disputes. Individuals will regularly inspect assigned facilities and equipment to ensure that cleaning standards are maintained and equipment is functioning appropriately. Individuals will assist in the hiring and training of team members. Individuals will participate in activities and functions as directed by the leadership of the department. Non-Student Hourly Research We provide a high-quality education to our diverse student population through excellence and innovation in teaching and research in order to serve the scientific and engineering needs of the state of Texas and the nation. This will be achieved by a balance of formal course work, practical laboratory training, and research projects that encompass both the basic science and the applied aspects of materials science and engineering. Before you leave, please sign up for our talent network! First Name (required) 502165f5 Last Name (required) 0bfccd54 Email (required) 65a1c14f Phone Number (optional) d13eab62 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) \u00c5land Islands (+358) Albania