rbia (+381) Seychelles (+248) Sierra Leone (+232) Singapore (+65) Sint Maarten (+1) Slovakia (+421) Slovenia (+386) Solomon Islands (+677) Somalia (+252) South Africa (+27) South Korea (+82) South Sudan (+211) Spain (+34) Sri Lanka (+94) St. Barth\u00e9lemy (+590) St. Helena (+290) St. Kitts & Nevis (+1) St. Lucia (+1) St. Martin (+590) St. Pierre & Miquelon (+508) St. Vincent & Grenadines (+1) Sudan (+249) Suriname (+597) Svalbard & Jan Mayen (+47) Sweden (+46) Switzerland (+41) Syria (+963) Taiwan (+886) Tajikistan (+992) Tanzania (+255) Thailand (+66) Timor-Leste (+670) Togo (+228) Tokelau (+690) Tonga (+676) Trinidad & Tobago (+1) Tunisia (+216) T\u00fcrkiye (+90) Turkmenistan (+993) Turks & Caicos Islands (+1) Tuvalu (+688) U.S. Virgin Islands (+1) Uganda (+256) Ukraine (+380) Uni"}, "https://careers.untsystem.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-clinical-psychology-denton-texas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology", "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology - Denton, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology - Denton, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology 515035 Denton, Texas, United States Faculty Title: Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Employee Classification: Asst Professor Campus: University of North Texas Division: UNT-Provost SubDivision-Department: UNT-Col of Publ Affairs & Hlth Sci Department: UNT-Psychology-122500 Job Location: Denton Salary: Compensation is competitive and commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and discipline, in accordance with university guidelines and available funding. FTE: 1.00 Retirement Eligibility: Not Retirement Eligible About Us - Values Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The UNT Department of Psychology is one of the largest and most dynamic psychology programs in the region, home to more than 40 faculty members, 100 graduate students, and over 2,500 undergraduate majors. Our faculty lead innovative research programs spanning clinical science, counseling psychology, cognitive and brain sciences, developmental psychology, health psychology, and social and behavioral health. Through mentorship, hands-on research training, and interdisciplinary collaboration, our students develop the knowledge and experience needed to succeed in academia, healthcare, industry, and public service. The Department of Psychology is housed within the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences (PAHS). PAHS prepares graduates to address diverse and complex social issues such as aging, disability, disaster management and recovery, criminal justice, health disparities, behavioral health, and public safety, and find solutions to challenges in public administration, public and mental health, exercise physiology, and urban design. PAHS has nine academic departments with undergraduate and graduate programs, and is also the home for several centers such as the UNT Center for Sport Psychology and Athlete Mental Health, the UNT Psychology Clinic, the Center for Psychosocial Health Disparities Research, the Kristin Farmer Autism Center, the Center for Public Management, the UNT Speech and Hearing Center, the UNT Work Inclusion and Supported Employment (UNTWISE) program, UNT ELEVAR (Empower, Learn, Excel, enVision, Advance, Rise), and several professional development and clinical training programs to facilitate careers to address a global society. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The Department of Psychology in the College of Public Affairs and Health Sciences at the University of North Texas invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology to join our APA-accredited doctoral program. We seek an innovative scholar whose research advances the understanding, prevention, assessment, or treatment of mental health conditions across the lifespan. The successful candidate will establish an externally funded research program while playing a key role in educating and mentoring doctoral students preparing for careers in clinical practice, research, and academia. This is an exceptional opportunity to join one of the nation's leading public research universities, where faculty are encouraged to pursue groundbreaking research, interdisciplinary collaboration, and community-engaged scholarship that advances mental health and well-being. The successful candidate will complement the department\u2019s existing strengths in health disparities, diagnosis and assessment, forensic psychology, post-traumatic stress disorder, neuropsychology, substance use disorders, and psychotherapy outcome research. Applicants employing innovative methodologies, including longitudinal research, clinical trials, community-engaged research, digital health technologies, implementation science, psychophysiology or advanced quantitative methods\u2014are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will: \u2022 Develop and sustain an externally funded research program in clinical psychology. \u2022 Teach doctoral- and undergraduate-level courses in clinical psychology and related areas. \u2022 Mentor doctoral students in research, clinical training, and professional development. \u2022 Supervise doctoral research, including master's theses and doctoral dissertations. \u2022 Contribute to clinical training through practicum supervision and other training experiences, consistent with the faculty member's expertise. \u2022 Publish impactful research in leading peer-reviewed journals and present findings at national and international conferences. \u2022 Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to address complex mental and behavioral health challenges. \u2022 Contribute to curriculum development, APA accreditation activities, departmental governance, and professional service. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology from an APA-accredited program or a closely related discipline. \u2022 Eligibility for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Texas. \u2022 Evidence of a strong and growing research agenda with potential for sustained external funding. \u2022 Demonstrated record of scholarly publications. \u2022 Commitment to excellence in teaching, mentoring, and training students. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Postdoctoral research or clinical training. \u2022 Experience mentoring undergraduate or graduate researchers. \u2022 Experience supervising clinical trainees. \u2022 Interest in interdisciplinary collaborations addressing complex mental health challenges. Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions Join Us! We're seeking a collaborative scholar who is passionate about advancing the science of mental health while mentoring the next generation of clinical psychologists. If you're excited to build an impactful research program, contribute to exceptional doctoral training, and translate scientific discovery into evidence-based practice, we invite you to apply. Review of applications will begin on 11/1/2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicant Documents \u2022 Cover Letter \u2022 Curriculum Vitae \u2022 Statement of Teaching Philosophy \u2022 Statement of Research Interests \u2022 Three reprints of peer reviewed articles \u2022 References \u2013 List of Names and Contact Information for 3 individuals Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation or proceeding. Apply for This Job First Name (required) d88f32b2 Last Name (required) 8565bb53 Email (required) e64aafe2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert f8cae26a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments UNT-Provost UNT-Provost Locations Denton, Texas, United States Denton, Texas, United States First Name (required) 2eceb428 Last Name (required) 24c3e877 Email (required) fcb92ddb Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) a76e3c0c Last Name (required) 75c4ee74 Email (required) 5310f34c Share to: a4e2cf24 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Recommended Jobs CAAAM Lab Assistant The CAAAM Lab Assistant role assists with experiments using techniques such as optical microscopy, profilometry, hardness testing, and density measurements, and helps translate experimental results into graphs and schematics. Additional responsibilities include maintaining laboratory inventory, coordinating incoming and outgoing packages, and following established laboratory safety practices. The ideal candidate will work effectively in a collaborative team environment, adapt to changing priorities, and demonstrate the ability to quickly learn new techniques and research solutions using relevant scientific literature. Completion of required UNT Lab Safety training is expected prior to beginning laboratory work. This is a temporary position with a start date of January 4, 2027 and ends on May 28, 2027 Office Support Assistant (Night Desk Clerk) The Office Support Assistant serves the full time staff member at the front desk overnight, providing a welcoming, safe, and secure environment for residents of the community. This position reports crisis and maintenance issues to on-call staff while providing customer support and other administrative follow-up. Custodian This position\u2019s purpose is to serve as a custodian for the Department of Housing and Residence Life. This is an essential position, maintaining essential operations during emergencies and university closures. The custodian will maintain a standard of cleanliness, sanitation, safety and standard of excellence in all assigned buildings (Residence Halls, Dining Areas, and Other Buildings). Associate Registrar This position is responsible for strategic oversight of Certifications and Degree Conferral, including planning, organizing, and ensuring continuity and continuous improvement of processes, systems, and student services including the maintenance and coordination of student, academic and curricular records to support enrollment and retention. Involved in new initiatives with colleagues across campus related to enrollment and retention to ensure successful implementation. Oversees operations of multiple functional areas and works directly with staff for ongoing professional development and the implementation of new initiatives, and/or updated systems, policies, and processes. Advises students, parents, faculty and staff about departmental and university regulations. Requires discernment to resolve complex escalations and implement proactive solutions. This position manages teams within the Office of the Registrar, collaborates across the division, and with faculty and staff throughout the University. Works to ensure the accuracy and integrity of academic and student data, and compliance with a range of institutional, state, and federal regulations. Responsible for collaboration across teams to achieve a collective outcome that optimizes results and impact that directly affects enrollment and retention. Custodial Services Supervisor This is an essential position, who's primary purpose is to provide direct supervision of the day-to-day operations of custodial staff within the residence halls, residential dining areas, and assigned auxiliary buildings. Supervisory responsibilities include: approving leave, managing time and attendance. Additionally, individuals will provide training, instruction, and coaching. Individuals will apply progressive discipline to subordinate staff as needed, in accordance with university, system, state and federal guidelines. Individuals will manage work teams of custodians to achieve cleaning goals, including managing interpersonal conflicts and resolving disputes. Individuals will regularly inspect assigned facilities and equipment to ensure that cleaning standards are maintained and equipment is functioning appropriately. Individuals will assist in the hiring and training of team members. Individuals will participate in activities and functions as directed by the leadership of the department. Non-Student Hourly Research We provide a high-quality education to our diverse student population through excellence and innovation in teaching and research in order to serve the scientific and engineering needs of the state of Texas and the nation. This will be achieved by a balance of formal course work, practical laboratory training, and research projects that encompass both the basic science and the applied aspects of materials science and engineering. Before you leave, please sign up for our talent network! First Name (required) ce9b3afa Last Name (required) 5dfe7fdd Email (required) cef79682 Phone Number (optional) 9e085c46 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) \u00c5land Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+5