r Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science - Denton, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science - Denton, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science Assistant or Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science 515316 Denton, Texas, United States Faculty Title: Assistant or Associate Professor: Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Science Employee Classification: Assoc Professor Campus: University of North Texas Division: UNT-Provost SubDivision-Department: UNT-College of Science Department: UNT-College of Science - Gen-124000 Job Location: Denton Salary: Compensation is competitive and commensurate with the candidate\u2019s qualifications, experience, and discipline, in accordance with university guidelines and available funding. FTE: 1.00 Retirement Eligibility: ORP Eligible About Us - Values Overview Welcome to the University of North Texas System. The UNT System includes the University of North Texas in Denton and Frisco, the University of North Texas at Dallas and UNT Dallas College of Law, and University of North Texas Health Fort Worth. We are the only university system based exclusively in the robust Dallas-Fort Worth region. We are growing with the North Texas region, employing more than 14,000 employees, educating a record 49,000+ students across our system, and awarding nearly 12,000 degrees each year. We are one team comprised of individuals who are committed to excellence, curiosity and innovation. We are transforming lives and creating economic opportunity through education. We champion a people-first values-based culture where We Care about each other and those we serve. We believe that we are Better Together because we foster an environment of respect, belonging, and access for all. We demonstrate Courageous Integrity through setting exceptional standards and acting in the best interest of our communities. We are encouraged to Be Curious about opportunities for learning, creating, discovering, and innovating, and are encouraged to learn from failure. Show Your Fire by joining our team and exhibiting your passion and pride in your work as part of our UNT System team. Learn more about the UNT System and how we live our values at www.UNTSystem.edu . Department Summary The University of North Texas (UNT) is a Carnegie R1 research university and a federally designated Hispanic-Serving Institution and Minority-Serving Institution with a population of over 45,000 students. The Denton, Texas community combines close proximity to one of the fastest growing metropolitan areas in the country (Dallas-Fort Worth) with an intimate and culturally vibrant college town atmosphere. The College of Science at the University of North Texas is a research-intensive unit that contributes to discoveries in both basic and applied sciences, with a strong and growing culture of interdisciplinary collaboration. In addition to upholding its strong research mission, the departments within the College of Science (Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, and Physics) are committed to delivering high-quality instruction that meets the needs of our student population of undergraduate and graduate students. Many of these students are interested in pursuing careers across a wide range of fields, with health-related professions representing a significant area of interest. Further information about the College of Science may be found at cos.unt.edu. UNT has a highly diverse campus with a wide range of languages spoken in addition to English. We welcome candidates who have experience with HSI/MSIs and/or who speak Spanish, Vietnamese, American Sign Language, Chinese (Cantonese, Mandarin and other variations), Arabic, Tagalog, Farsi, French, or/and Yoruba. Position Overview The UNT College of Science invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor with a focus on artificial intelligence in biomedical science, to begin September 1, 2027. Applicants should have a record of research accomplishment and compelling ideas for building an independent research program that is focused on the application of AI and computational modeling for studying the function and interactions of biological macromolecules and processes. The research should be grounded in one or more natural science disciplines that exist within COS (biological sciences, chemistry, and physics), and research in highly interdisciplinary directions is encouraged. Possible directions within the broader biomedical research field include drug discovery, biomolecular design, disease diagnosis and treatment, and elucidating mechanisms of disease, among others. This position is part of a Biomedical Research Cluster Hire which aims to recruit five new faculty members with expertise in health- and cancer-related research\u2014encompassing cancer biology, microbiome research, medical biophysics, and chemical oncology\u2014to the UNT College of Science in Fall 2027. The selected individual will be appointed to one or more academic departments within COS and will interact with researchers across the university, including the BioDiscovery Institute and the Biomedical Engineering Department, contributing to planned growth in interdisciplinary health-related research at UNT. Development of a nationally and internationally visible, externally funded research program is expected. The new faculty member will receive a competitive startup package and will have access to existing computing resources at UNT. Contributions to undergraduate and graduate teaching (typically, one course per long semester) and departmental and university service are expected. Review of applications will begin November 10, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 A Ph.D. in Biology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, Chemical Biology, Physics, or a closely related field. \u2022 A record of peer-reviewed publications related to artificial intelligence and/or machine learning. \u2022 Employees in this job may be responsible for conducting research on, working on, or having the ability to access critical organizational infrastructure and they must be able to maintain the security and integrity of the infrastructure related to this role. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience \u2022 A record of peer-reviewed publications with strong relevance to biomedical research Required License/Registration/Certifications Physical Requirements Communicating with others to exchange information. Environmental Hazards No adverse environmental conditions expected. Work Schedule varies based on assignment Driving University Vehicle No Security Sensitive This is a Security Sensitive Position. Special Instructions Applicants should provide the following as part of their applications. \u2022 A Cover Letter summarizing your qualifications and interest in the position \u2022 A Curriculum Vitae \u2022 As your Statement of Research Interests, please attach a research proposal (suggested length: 3 pages) \u2022 Statement of Teaching Philosophy (maximum of 2 pages) \u2022 Names and contact information for three professional references \u2013 UNT will notify you before contacting them \u2022 Transcripts are not required at the time of application, but it is helpful to include them if available Benefits For information regarding our Benefits, click here . EEO Statement The University of North Texas System is firmly committed to equal opportunity and does not permit \u2013and takes actions to prevent \u2013 discrimination, harassment (including sexual violence, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking), and retaliation on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its application, employment practices, and facilities; nor permits race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran status, or sex discrimination and harassment in its admissions processes, and educational programs and activities. UNT System Administration promptly investigates complaints of discrimination, harassment, and related retaliation and takes remedial action when appropriate. System Administration also takes actions to prevent retaliation against individuals who oppose any form of harassment or discriminatory practice, file a charge or report, or testify, assist, or participate in a related investigation or proceeding. Apply for This Job First Name (required) 847c3c31 Last Name (required) f9a90148 Email (required) 8c591995 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert cb5dc1ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments UNT-Provost UNT-Provost Locations Denton, Texas, United States Denton, Texas, United States First Name (required) f6ec2633 Last Name (required) 9b731dc7 Email (required) 2b83fe83 Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Want to Share This Job? First Name (required) 9c6fe918 Last Name (required) a1b8d90f Email (required) 9b25b99e Share to: f2e6087d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at the University of North Texas System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Director Enrollment Communications & Engagement The Senior Director Enrollment Communications & Engagement is a division level position that leads the planning, implementation, and oversight of internal and external communications in support of the mission, priorities, and goals of the Division and the University. In alignment with the vision and direction of divisional leadership, the role advances communication strategies, oversees messaging and engagement efforts, promotes standards and best practices, and evaluates outcomes to strengthen effectiveness, consistency, and user experience across communication channels. This position leads cross-functional initiatives, supports strategic priorities, and ensures communication efforts are aligned with institutional messaging, branding expectations, and UNT System policies and procedures. Research Development Specialist The Research Development Specialist provides administrative, logistical, and operational support to the Research Development team within the Division of Research and Innovation at the University of North Texas. Reporting to the Associate Director of Research Development, this position assists with the planning, implementation, and evaluation of Research Development workshops, events, programs, and initiatives that support faculty research activity. The position works collaboratively with Research Development leadership and staff to support established research development programs, maintain organized and accurate information, and ensure the timely execution of assigned duties to support operations of the team. Responsibilities include supporting event logistics and registration; identifying and disseminating research funding opportunities; coordinating targeted faculty outreach; preparing and distributing departmental communications; maintaining Research Development web content and resources; monitoring shared email inboxes; assisting with faculty research funding inquiries; and maintaining departmental tracking systems for data reporting. Donated Body Administrative Associate This position will serve as the Donated Body Program Administrative Associate and will be handling the mailing and processing of new membership applications, filing of death certificates, and supporting program leadership with other administrative tasks. Associate Director, Career Services The Associate Director Career Services is responsible for preparing students for internships within the community and engaging with area employers to stay up to date on the needs of their workforce. This person coaches individual students through process, facilitates group-level workshops such as mock-interviews, networking opportunities, and creation of personal brand artifacts as well as serves as instructor of internship courses for multi-disciplinary programs at the UNT at Frisco campus. This position also supervises two Career and Employer Development Specialists who serve all majors at the Frisco campus. Assistant General Counsel The University of North Texas System Office of General Counsel has an immediate opening for an Assistant General Counsel to join a dedicated team of attorneys and professional staff. The UNT System includes the System Administration, the University of North Texas, the University of North Texas Health Science Center at Fort Worth, and the University of North Texas at Dallas. The UNT System Office of General Counsel includes ten attorneys and seven professional staff located in offices on the institutional campuses and at the UNT System building in downtown Dallas. The Assistant General Counsel will provide legal advice and services to UNT System and its component institutions as a member of the System Office of General Counsel. The primary office location for this position is located on the UNT campus in Denton, Texas. This position also requires as-needed travel to UNT System locations and may include limited hybrid work opportunities as well. This position will manage the public information process. It is estimated that 30%-35% of the workload will be supporting the public information office and providing legal services in connection with the release of public information and responses to records requests. In addition, this position is a generalist position that handles matters in the areas of academic affairs, student affairs, administrative law, general risk management and insurance, policy review and legislation analysis, litigation support, ethics and conflicts of interest, HR/employment law, FLSA, FMLA, EEOC, information management, regulatory and compliance matters such as the Clery Act, FERPA, Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, and general higher education issues. As an office that is fully committed to exceptional representation, the UNT System Office of General Counsel works collaboratively to deliver advice to our higher education clients in an atmosphere of trust and respect. The successful candidate is expected to have an appreciation for the mission of higher education, a commitment to excellence and proactive lawyering, an enthusiasm for client outreach, and a passion for professional development and growth. Director, Data Management & Business Intelligence This technical leadership position directs DAIR data management, data quality, master data management, institutional definitions and data stewardship. The Director oversees analytical data modelling, integration, validation, and business intelligence products that make university information reliable, accessible and usable. The role leads development of dashboards and data visualizations for faculty, institutional reporting and benchmarking, and guides DAIR requirements and quality assurance during modernization of SAS-based analytics to Microsoft Fabric or other approved tools. The Director supervises assigned staff, sets operational priorities, resolves data issues with institutional partners, and contributes to DAIR strategic planning and delivery. Training and user enablement support adoption of these products but are not the primary purpose of the position. Before you leave, please sign up for our talent network! First Name (required) b693c75a Last Name (required) 120b7d2e Email (required) fb57cc09 Phone Number (optional) 1acf24cf 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) \u00c5land Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) C\u00f4te d\u2019Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Cura\u00e7ao (+599) Cyprus (+357) 